A cybersecurity learning game where you are the packet.
Concept Overview

Packet Runner is a browser-based cybersecurity game where the player takes on the role of a data packet traveling through a hostile digital network.

The goal is simple in theory but chaotic in execution:

Reach the destination server alive while surviving real-world inspired cyber threats.

Instead of swords or guns, your enemies are:

Malware clusters 
Phishing traps 
Firewalls & filters 
DDoS storm zones 
Corrupted nodes & spoofed routes 

And your upgrades are cybersecurity concepts:

Encryption keys 
VPN tunnels 
Security patches 
Authentication tokens 

🎮 Gameplay Core Loop
Spawn as a data packet
Navigate network nodes (routes)
Avoid or bypass cyber threats
Collect security tools (buffs)
Reach destination server
Learn the concept behind each obstacle

Each mission teaches a real cybersecurity principle disguised as gameplay.

