🗺️ Mission Progress (So Far)

The game is structured in missions (training chapters):

✅ Mission 001: Packet Awakening
Introduction to packet identity
Basic movement through network nodes
✅ Mission 002: Basic Routing
Learning path selection
Avoiding simple dead nodes
✅ Mission 003: Phishing Trap Awareness
Introduction to fake nodes / spoofed paths
Teaching user verification instincts
✅ Mission 004: Malware Zone
First encounter with infected nodes
Basic avoidance mechanics
✅ Mission 005: Firewall Barrier
Understanding blocked routes
Learning permission-based navigation
🔄 Mission 006: Firewall Breach / Secure Passage
Advanced firewall behavior
Timing + pattern-based traversal
Intro to secure tunneling concepts
🚧 Mission 007 (Planned): Source Tracking Protocol
Packet learns to trace origin of compromised routes
Introduces attacker source identification logic
Early threat intelligence concept

Design Philosophy

Packet Runner is built around one idea:

“If you can play cybersecurity, you can understand cybersecurity.”

Instead of memorizing terms, players experience attacks in motion.

Think:

Less textbook 
More digital survival simulation 
Visual Direction
Neon cyber grid aesthetic 
Dark network void background
Glowing packet trails
Corrupted zones flickering like broken signals
Clean UI overlays (terminal-inspired)

